watch": "Any independent spending on Wellman's behalf or a second independent poll confirming a tie would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Ann Wagner (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ann Wagner seeks another term in Missouri's 2nd District, a seat that leans Republican by about four points, against Democrat Fred Wellman, a former Army officer and political newcomer. Wagner holds a decisive financial edge, with roughly $4.2 million on hand compared with Wellman's $242,000, and no significant outside spending has entered the race on either side.\n\nStill, the race looks closer than a typical incumbent contest. A September poll from a Republican-leaning firm showed Wagner up just one point, and several ratings outlets call it a Tossup while others say Lean or Likely Republican. The evidence points to a narrow Wagner advantage with meaningful uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2379, "margin": -4.26}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2517, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2424, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2065, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.22, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1903, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2785, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3439, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3337, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3474, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3466, "margin": -3.0}]}